                      "name": "Many Note Body",
                      "fill": "$text-secondary",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Each chart scrolls its own rows. The card heading, the axis labels and the Now line are pinned above the scroll area, so an account far down the list is measured against the same shared axis. Equal windows are equal widths, shifted only by when that account's window started, which makes the rows directly comparable. Both charts keep the same account order. The companion window itself never scrolls — only the two row areas do.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                      "fontSize": 10.5,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
